---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { settings } from '../lib/settings';
---
<Layout title="Contact & corrections" description="Contact the MyJourney publisher about editorial questions, corrections, or privacy requests for the website and serversiderestu app.">
  <div class="container policy-page">
    <header class="page-heading">
      <p class="eyebrow">Contact & corrections</p>
      <h1>Help make a guide<br/>more useful.</h1>
      <p>Questions, factual corrections, and privacy requests belong here.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>Reach the publisher</h2>
      <p>Email <a class="text-link" href={`mailto:${settings.contactEmail}`}>{settings.contactEmail}</a> for editorial questions, corrections, or privacy requests about this website or the serversiderestu app. This opens your email application; this website does not collect a contact-form submission.</p>
      <p>For a privacy request, say whether it concerns MyJourney or serversiderestu and include only the details needed to identify the issue. Do not send Pinterest access tokens, app secrets, passwords, or other sensitive credentials. Read the <a class="text-link" href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> for the website and app’s data practices.</p>
      <h2>Make a correction easy to review</h2>
      <p>Include the article URL, the passage you want reviewed, and a short explanation. A link to the relevant manufacturer documentation or another original source helps resolve a factual question. For device compatibility, include the exact model rather than a general product name.</p>
      <p>Send only the information needed to understand the issue. Avoid passwords, payment information, private account details, and other sensitive records.</p>
      <h2>Orders and product support</h2>
      <p>{settings.brand} publishes editorial guides. We do not process purchases, deliveries, returns, or warranties. Direct those questions to the seller or product manufacturer through their own support channels.</p>
      <h2>How corrections are handled</h2>
      <p>A proposed factual correction needs a source review before it changes an article. Material corrections should explain what changed and show the actual revision date. Read the <a class="text-link" href="/editorial-policy/">editorial policy</a> for the full approach.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
